{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RE-CLOSE-0059-A: re-closed on its own merits through a gate that can now see\n\nReopened because the original close carried no completion-verifier attestation. Re-verified both\nacceptance criteria independently before re-closing; neither rests on the epic's need to certify.\n\n**AC1 — mechanism identified and cited, and the 5f48-duplicate question settled.** The reported\nsymptom (`scanned=1 filed=0`, \"no local ticket created from DC issue\") was real; its stated cause was\nnot. The defect was in the test's own oracle, not in inbound filing:\n\n  * `_jira_key_to_local_id` lowercases (`inbound_translate.py:120-124`), so `RBJNAZV-1` becomes\n    `jira-rbjnazv-1` and the cell's case-sensitive `remote_key in json.dumps(t)` scan could not match;\n  * the inbound CREATE payload (`apply_inbound_records.py:183-212`) carries no raw Jira key at all —\n    the key appears only as a title fallback, unused whenever the issue has a summary.\n\nSo the oracle could not distinguish a perfectly-created ticket from a missing one in EITHER direction.\nSeparately, `filed` counts invariant-violation bug tickets (`run_differs.py:282`,\n`check_at_most_one_local_id`), so `filed=0` was healthy and said nothing about inbound at all.\n\nNot a duplicate of 5f48 (the silent identity-mint failure) — that was the filing ticket's own candidate\nhypothesis and it is wrong. It IS the same underlying issue as [rebar:23ed-de0a-765b-49aa], which\ndiagnosed it to this cause and fixed it (merged as change 1124). Closing as a duplicate of 23ed.\n\n**AC2 — the cell passes against the live DC harness.** `executed=17 skipped=0`, with\n`test_a_dc_created_ticket_carries_the_shared_jira_provenance` passing on an assertion that now has\nreach: exact equality against `_jira_key_to_local_id(remote_key)`, the binding store mapping that local\nid to the DC key, and `creation_channel == \"jira\"`. The `skipped=0` matters as much as the pass count.\n\nNo inbound-filing defect exists. Three defects had masked this assertion in sequence — an empty store\nreporting `scanned=0`, the PAT-cap bug [rebar:f391-806b-938f-45d8] killing setup, then the oracle itself\n— which is why the verdict only became informative once all three were fixed."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785861241887333001,"uuid":"8e3d3ff2-1324-4f7e-80ad-6341cbd8d7ff"}